      children: "Configuration Drift in Hybrid Teams"
    }), "\n", _jsx(_components.p, {
      children: "When multiple teams share a Kong instance, configuration drift becomes a serious operational risk. Without rigorous GitOps enforcement, production configuration diverges from the declarative files in version control. The Admin API is powerful and easy to invoke - it takes discipline to prevent ad-hoc changes that never get committed back to the repository."
    }), "\n", _jsxs(_components.p, {
      children: ["The solution is to treat the Admin API as write-protected in production. All changes flow through pull requests to the declarative config files, validated by a CI pipeline that runs ", _jsx(_components.code, {
        children: "deck diff"
      }), " (Kong's declarative configuration tool) against the running instance before applying. The ", _jsx(_components.code, {
        children: "deck"
      }), " CLI makes this tractable: ", _jsx(_components.code, {
        children: "deck sync"
      }), " applies the diff between the declared config and the live state, and ", _jsx(_components.code, {
        children: "deck dump"
      }), " exports current live config for auditing."]
